import AFTD.Prelude

/-!
# simple_graph_is_hop

Topic: graphs   Node: 3987b76073c4

Provenance: formalization of a published result. Source: arXiv:2610.18463 (The group generated by a graph's derangements), Sec. 1 (definition of a hop; called a graph derangement in earlier work).

A hop (graph derangement) of a graph G is a permutation h of the vertices that sends every vertex v to a neighbour h(v) of v.
-/

/-- A hop of `G`: a permutation sending every vertex to one of its neighbours. -/
def simple_graph_is_hop {V : Type*} (G : SimpleGraph V) (h : Equiv.Perm V) : Prop :=
  ∀ v, G.Adj v (h v)
